    "body": "Answers from the machine owner (Sodick AQ600L, LN2W control), 2026-11-25. These close the open questions above.\n\n- **`G29`:** It is not required. It marks a restart point. If the wire does not thread at a start hole, the control skips forward to the next `G29`. This is useful for a batch of parts.\n- **Condition and offset numbers:** `C001` is always the first cutting condition, and it always goes with `H001`. For a later pass n (`H00n`), the condition number is not always `C00n`. It comes from the operator's condition table.\n- The same `G41`/`G42 H` scheme, `G40` on a lead-out move and C/H pairing apply to other wire EDM makes with small changes.\n\nConsequence for the work:\n- Write `G41`/`G42 Hnnn` on its own line before the lead-in. H is the pass number from `H001`.\n- Write `C001` with `H001` for the first pass. For later passes, write the condition that the operation states. Do not compute `C00n` from the pass number.\n- `G29` is optional. Do not write it by default.\n\n#4065 merged on 2026-11-26, so this work can start from `main`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
